<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qianlong Emperor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Qianlong Emperor ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> from 1735 to 1796, presiding over its greatest territorial extent. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-great-campaigns">Ten Great Campaigns</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungaria">Dzungaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-turkestan">Eastern Turkestan</a> and reached into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. His reign was also marked by a literary inquisition that suppressed texts considered subversive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qianlong-emperor.jpg" alt="Qianlong Emperor" width="316" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Castiglione · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%B9%BE%E9%9A%86%E7%9A%87%E5%B8%9D%E6%9C%9D%E6%9C%8D%E5%83%8F%E8%BD%B4.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
